    "responsibility": "Complete input-owner refinement across authored action-context view closure, original historical source, deliberately mutable test snapshots, immutable output fixtures, verified installed ASCENT package resources and all three native attestation consumers.",
    "retired": "Assumptions that the registered view inventory includes every explicit context dependency, that copied mutable files retain the original repository identity, that output-source locators survive transfer without their Git owner, and that every native DSL resource is a repository-relative file. Fixture author no longer relies on global Git settings.",
    "validation": "137 scoped passes, zero skips: complete source12, real-source-impact10, submission36, native-review68 modules and complete ProgressiveClueTests11 previously absent IDs. Those11 actual IDs equal the original075 missing set. Their other38 CLI tests and full CI remain independent. Original entry-view refusal reproduces; candidate discover passes with unchanged facts/ranges/SHA. Wrong owner/blob/source drift, missing output origin, UTF8/source-generation refusal and original full-module assertions remain. Native-review uses original60s sealed policy,5.505s.11 cases use existing execute and standard unittest isolated processes,68.793s under unchanged120s whole qualification cap. Initial serial120s failures, missing fixture dependencies and denied unregistered sealed-provider loading remain retained.",
    "benefits": "Original studies now read original objects independently of current modular runtime source. Mutable fixtures receive explicit ownership from real declared bytes and still prove source edits reopen affected summaries. Immutable output transfer borrows only the actual object owner without source/checkout duplication. Verified installed inputs retain canonical package labels even outside project root; unknown external owners refuse. All three regular/unavailable/relation consumers share one label contract.",
    "costs": "Three Git descriptors and exact object/hash reads; one shared mutable initializer, one object-borrow helper and one API-owner label projection. Per-input digest checks and fixture-local metadata remain necessary. The same API owner inventory is reused within its original checked lifetime, not a global validation cache. Six isolated qualification processes use existing capacity accounting; this is not a new public executor. No runtime throughput or total peak improvement measured; no heap, wait, native workspace or CI-budget increase.",
    "process": "One complete source/fixture/package ownership support unit based on075d5c2c, progressDelta0. Modern-c runtime head3d42 remains unchanged. Architecture locally3/4 with one complete result remaining; independent SMP1/12 with11 tests remaining. Fourth integration stays blocked by independent source/product/remote prerequisites.",
    "checklist": "dev/refactoring/modern-c/input-owners.org#input-owners",
    "models": "Native SysML owns explicit owner roles, all three consumers, historical/mutable/installed boundaries and five ASCENT needs, and derives D2 through native tools. Existing ASCENT admission consumes source-bound test observations and this matrix. QNT owns schedule/epoch properties and Lean conditional algebra; neither is duplicated for source/host refinement. LLM review supplies source correspondence, never native or hosted facts.",
    "open": "Current075 full framework remains DENY:2417 expected,2406 run,40 failures,31 errors,2 skips and11 absent IDs; all71 failure/error identities equal6fa, while scoped original11 pass locally. Complete current framework rerun and remaining38 CLI tests not qualified here. Old7c source-provisioning checkout/index proof versus modern3d, retired projections, other full-framework contracts and causal-review source epochs stay open. Upstream-check rejects original os_setup and table-model references; original objects located, no current causal approval inferred or SHA refreshed. Hosted macOS pair remains queued. Build/five module passes are a locked repair-source cohort, not modern-c runtime credit. No scheduler or fourth-result work is mixed in."
